From 9bcaa3331fe28c9a8366842b4b9672c82c651c04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armaghan Ahmad Shad <armaghanahmadshad@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 01:37:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Content sync, code-splitting, lint cleanup, new blog post

- Lazy-load routes (React.lazy/Suspense) to cut initial bundle from
  501KB to 452KB; admin dashboard and blog posts now ship as
  on-demand chunks instead of in the main bundle.
- Sync real content: Hero stats (40+ certs, 6 projects, 12+ tools),
  About timeline (add NeuroFive internship + MSA role), Projects
  (add Smart Campus Automation System, MediFlow, Apna ChatBot,
  Live Crypto Pulse to the existing 2).
- Add supabase/seed_real_data.sql with real certificates + skills
  data, ready to run in the Supabase SQL editor (certificates/skills
  are DB-driven, so this can't be pushed programmatically without
  project credentials).
- New blog post: 'From AZ-900 to AZ-104' covering the Azure/AWS
  cloud fundamentals learning path, wired into routing + blog list.
- Lint cleanup: removed unused default React imports across ~20
  files (React 19 + Vite's automatic JSX runtime doesn't need them);
  documented eslint-disable for 3 false-positive set-state-in-effect
  warnings on a standard fetch-on-mount pattern in AdminDashboard.
